{
  "id": "march-seed",
  "title": "A seeded march never skips an occluder that moved in front of its history's surface",
  "binding": "The positive leg boots a striped backdrop at native render scale with world.temporal and world.march-seed on, and a red SDF slab four units aside. Once the history holds the backdrop, a seat-granted edit submitted at tick 64 moves the slab in front of it on tick 65, and the world view is captured at tick 65: every pixel there proposes the backdrop's distance as its march's start, which the ball test must refuse across the slab. A camera view of the same eye and target, which never seeds, renders the spatial path and is captured at tick 66. Over the slab both captures show the slab in every pixel, and the seeded capture differs from the unseeded one by at most 4 codes. The discriminating leg submits the edit one tick later, so the tick 65 capture still shows the backdrop where the slab lands and both claims fail.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
  "fixtures": [],
